 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope; issue #93 defines the aggregate usage delivered after tool rounds.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+- A turn in which some provider calls report usage and others do not reports the total of the calls that did, and a turn in which no call reports usage still reports `undefined` ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- `addUsage` adds each token field of a reported round to the running total, so the total is the sum over the provider calls that reported ([validated by: sums each token field across reported rounds](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L32)).
+- A provider call that reports no usage leaves the running total as it was, rather than making it `undefined` or `NaN` ([validated by: keeps the total when a round reported nothing](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36)).
+- When nothing has been reported yet, the first reported round becomes the total ([validated by: takes the round when nothing has been reported yet](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)).
+- A total stays `undefined` when no provider call reported usage, so a turn that reported nothing still reports nothing ([validated by: stays undefined when no round reported usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L44)).
